# Cursor Rules — Pare (NFL head-to-head comparison app)

## Source of truth
- **`CLAUDE.md` (repo root) is the single source of truth** for rules, architecture, data
  freshness, commands, and gotchas. This file is only the short always-on subset so scoped
  tasks don't need to load it. If anything here conflicts with `CLAUDE.md`, `CLAUDE.md` wins.

## Standing engineering rules (ALWAYS apply)
- Stack: Next.js 15.5 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind v4. Dev server on port 4000. Live at pare.gg.
- DARK MODE ONLY. Mobile-first — design at ~393px (iPhone 14 Pro); this web app is the base for an iOS app.
- TypeScript strict, no `any`; typed props/interfaces. Hooks hold logic; components render.
- Design tokens only (`docs/design-system.md`, values in `app/globals.css :root`). Never hardcode
  a color/radius/shadow; no raw Tailwind palette classes (CI fails on them).
- SURGICAL over rebuild: small, atomic, scoped to exactly what's asked. Don't refactor unrelated code.
- Do NOT change the data layer, the ranking / display-mode / bar-calculation math, or hook
  signatures unless the task explicitly says so. Preserve the theScore inward-bar logic.
- Comparison state lives in the comparisons store (`lib/comparisons/store.ts` +
  `ComparisonsProvider`); schedule state in `ScheduleProvider`. Don't add parallel state.
- Data: ESPN + Sleeper only (see DATA_SOURCES.md). Respect the freshness timers in `CLAUDE.md`
  → "Freshness" — one timer per data type, never nest `unstable_cache`, always keep a fallback
  so the app never blanks.
- Dead code → `_to-delete/<date>-<what>/`, never silently deleted.

## Verification (token-thrifty — important)
- Do NOT open a browser, drive it, or take screenshots to self-verify. Kobe checks the UI.
- Verify with cheap checks ONLY: `npm run check`, `npm run test:run`, curl + jq, row counts,
  internal-consistency assertions. Print the numbers, don't screenshot.

## When to read the big docs (don't by default)
- CLAUDE.md: read for architecture-level, data/caching, or cross-cutting work.
- DATA_SOURCES.md: read only when wiring or changing data endpoints.
- For a scoped, surgical change, these standing rules cover it.
- Do NOT print "Rule Summary / Ambiguities / Confirmation" blocks unless asked.

## Docs ritual (keep, but lightweight)
- Conventional Commits: feat: / fix: / refactor: / perf: / docs: / chore:.
- Non-trivial change → short Dev Note at docs/devnotes/YYYY-MM-DD-<task>.md
  (rationale only; link CLAUDE.md, don't duplicate it) + a CHANGELOG [Unreleased] bullet
  linking it. Skip the note for tiny one-line fixes.
- Create an ADR (docs/adr/) only for a genuine architectural decision.
- Promote a rule into CLAUDE.md only when it's reusable.
